# The counter is 32 bits and wraps; the meter reads it each second and
# takes the difference modulo 2^32, so a wrap between two reads is growth
# like any other. From 4294966296 (2^32 - 1000) to 4000 is 5000 bytes. The
# bandwidth is the growth over the last five seconds, divided by them:
# 5000 bytes a second here, and 0 once it has been still for five.
0 policy
snooping=1
igmp_function=0
immediate_leave=1
end
0 tick
1 v3join 1 10 192.168.1.10 239.2.2.2
1 ctr 239.2.2.2 4294956296
